## Running the demo

```sh
make demo   # python -m app.main --offline — mock ASR/TTS, synthetic transcript, no network
make eval   # score the scribe's extraction against the fixture set
make check  # compile-check + test the generated project
```

`make demo` never touches the network: ASR, TTS, and the model provider
are dispatched to their mocks, exactly as `ack demo --offline` does for
every agenticcarekit blueprint.

## Scope — read this before you extend it

This blueprint produces **decision support**: documentation drafting,
navigation, accessibility, triage *routing*, and patient education. It
does **not** diagnose and does **not** recommend or select treatment. If
you extend this app toward clinical judgment, you have left the scope
this template was designed and reviewed for — get a clinician and a
compliance review involved first.

All bundled sample data (transcripts, patient names, MRNs, vitals) is
synthetic or drawn from public FHIR test fixtures. Do not point this demo
at real PHI without first configuring a real redactor and a policy that
matches your organization's requirements.

## Ejectable: this is your code now

Nothing in this project imports "the framework" and calls back into it.
`app/` is plain Python that happens to import `agenticcarekit.kernel` and
`agenticcarekit.capabilities` the same way any other dependency is
imported. Delete `agenticcarekit` from `pyproject.toml`, inline the bits
you use, and it still runs. Generated once, owned forever.
